  "chain": "brazed bus-stud connection design lacked backing-wrench provision [cause B] -> torsional degradation of brazed stud connection over repeated maintenance -> open circuit fault at secondary bus connection -> HPCS transformer damaged -> loss of power to Division III 480 VAC switchgear -> HPCS inoperable / loss of initiation capability [backups RCIC, ADS, Division 1/2 ECCS available]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Standby Service Water Pump 2C (SWP-P2C) was also declared inoperable due to the same Division III power loss but is treated as a co-affected system rather than part of the HPCS causal chain, since the narrative does not detail its failure mechanism. Division 1 and Division 2 ECCS trains and ADS were stated operable and met 10 CFR 50.46 performance criteria while HPCS was out of service; RCIC was verified operable per the narrative and is modeled as a stated-operable backup along with ADS. No previous similar events were reported."
